{"id":"9ff7b1c114d80073b6156fa930260383ef8a75a0","axis":"silent","repo":"projectdiscovery/naabu","sha":"9ff7b1c114d80073b6156fa930260383ef8a75a0","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"README.md","lines":["@@ -92,6 +92,7 @@ OUTPUT:","    -oX, -xml-output string                write nmap-compatible XML output to file (- for stdout)","    -oG, -grep-output string               write nmap-compatible greppable output to file (- for stdout)","    -oA, -output-all string                write json, xml and greppable output to <basename>.{json,xml,gnmap}","+   -port-state                            also report closed and filtered tcp ports"," "," SERVICES-DISCOVERY:","    -sD, -service-discovery           identify services by port number"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"_typos.toml","lines":["@@ -4,3 +4,4 @@ nd = \"nd\""," AIMD = \"AIMD\""," # DefautStatsInterval is exported; renaming it breaks SDK callers"," Defaut = \"Defaut\"","+unparseable = \"unparseable\""],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pkg/result/results.go","lines":["@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@ package result"," import ("," \t\"context\""," \t\"fmt\"","+\t\"math/bits\""," \t\"net\""," \t\"os/exec\""," \t\"runtime\"","@@ -13,6 +14,7 @@ import ("," \t\"unicode\""," "," \t\"github.com/projectdiscovery/naabu/v2/pkg/port\"","+\t\"github.com/projectdiscovery/naabu/v2/pkg/protocol\""," \t\"github.com/projectdiscovery/naabu/v2/pkg/result/confidence\""," )"," ","@@ -41,6 +43,7 @@ type HostResult struct {"," type Result struct {"," \tsync.RWMutex"," \tipPorts   map[string]map[string]*port.Port","+\tclosed    map[string]*closedSet"," \tips       map[string]struct{}"," \tskipped   map[string]struct{}"," \tdeadHosts map[string]struct{}","@@ -52,6 +55,7 @@ type Result struct {"," func NewResult() *Result {"," \treturn &Result{"," \t\tipPorts:   make(map[string]map[string]*port.Port),","+\t\tclosed:    make(map[string]*closedSet),"," \t\tips:       make(map[string]struct{}),"," \t\tskipped:   make(map[string]struct{}),"," \t\tdeadHosts: make(map[string]struct{}),","@@ -163,6 +167,95 @@ func (r *Result) AddPort(ip string, p *port.Port) {"," "," \tr.ipPorts[ip][portIdentity(p)] = p"," \tr.ips[ip] = struct{}{}","+\tif set := r.closed[ip]; set != nil {","+\t\tset.remove(p)","+\t}","+}","+","+// closedSet holds the closed tcp ports of one host as a bitset. A scan of the","+// whole port range finds tens of thousands of closed ports per host, which a","+// map of port pointers would store at about 100 bytes each; the bitset is a","+// fixed 8 KiB per host.","+type closedSet struct {","+\tbits  [1 << 10]uint64","+\tcount int","+}","+","+func closedIndex(p *port.Port) (word int, mask uint64, ok bool) {","+\tif p == nil || p.Protocol != protocol.TCP || p.Port < 0 || p.Port > 65535 {","+\t\treturn 0, 0, false","+\t}","+\treturn p.Port >> 6, 1 << (uint(p.Port) & 63), true","+}","+","+func (c *closedSet) add(p *port.Port) {","+\tif word, mask, ok := closedIndex(p); ok && c.bits[word]&mask == 0 {","+\t\tc.bits[word] |= mask","+\t\tc.count++","+\t}","+}","+","+func (c *closedSet) remove(p *port.Port) {","+\tif word, mask, ok := closedIndex(p); ok && c.bits[word]&mask != 0 {","+\t\tc.bits[word] &^= mask","+\t\tc.count--","+\t}","+}","+","+func (c *closedSet) ports() []*port.Port {","+\tout := make([]*port.Port, 0, c.count)","+\tfor word, w := range &c.bits {","+\t\tfor ; w != 0; w &= w - 1 {","+\t\t\tout = append(out, &port.Port{Port: word<<6 + bits.TrailingZeros64(w), Protocol: protocol.TCP})","+\t\t}","+\t}","+\treturn out","+}","+","+// AddClosedPort records that ip answered the tcp port p with a reset. An open","+// reply wins over a reset whichever arrives first, so AddPort also clears the","+// port here. Ports that are not tcp are ignored.","+func (r *Result) AddClosedPort(ip string, p *port.Port) {","+\tif p == nil {","+\t\treturn","+\t}","+\tr.Lock()","+\tdefer r.Unlock()","+","+\tif _, open := r.ipPorts[ip][portIdentity(p)]; open {","+\t\treturn","+\t}","+\tset, ok := r.closed[ip]","+\tif !ok {","+\t\tset = &closedSet{}","+\t\tr.closed[ip] = set","+\t}","+\tset.add(p)","+}","+","+// GetClosedPorts returns the closed ports recorded per ip, in port order.","+func (r *Result) GetClosedPorts() map[string][]*port.Port {","+\tr.RLock()","+\tdefer r.RUnlock()","+","+\tout := make(map[string][]*port.Port, len(r.closed))","+\tfor ip, set := range r.closed {","+\t\tif set.count == 0 {","+\t\t\tcontinue","+\t\t}","+\t\tout[ip] = set.ports()","+\t}","+\treturn out","+}","+","+// MergeClosedPorts copies the closed ports of other into r, skipping any port","+// r holds open.","+func (r *Result) MergeClosedPorts(other *Result) {","+\tfor ip, ports := range other.GetClosedPorts() {","+\t\tfor _, p := range ports {","+\t\t\tr.AddClosedPort(ip, p)","+\t\t}","+\t}"," }"," "," // SetPorts for a specific ip","@@ -176,6 +269,9 @@ func (r *Result) SetPorts(ip string, ports []*port.Port) {"," "," \tfor _, p := range ports {"," \t\tr.ipPorts[ip][portIdentity(p)] = p","+\t\tif set := r.closed[ip]; set != nil {","+\t\t\tset.remove(p)","+\t\t}"," \t}"," \tr.ips[ip] = struct{}{}"," }","@@ -354,6 +450,22 @@ func (r *Result) GetHostPortsMap() map[string][]int {"," \treturn out"," }"," ","+// GetTCPPortCounts returns how many open tcp ports each ip has.","+func (r *Result) GetTCPPortCounts() map[string]int {","+\tr.RLock()","+\tdefer r.RUnlock()","+","+\tout := make(map[string]int, len(r.ipPorts))","+\tfor ip, ports := range r.ipPorts {","+\t\tfor _, p := range ports {","+\t\t\tif p.Protocol == protocol.TCP {","+\t\t\t\tout[ip]++","+\t\t\t}","+\t\t}","+\t}","+\treturn out","+}","+"," // GetPortCount returns the number of ports discovered for an ip"," func (r *Result) GetPortCount(host string) int {"," \tr.RLock()"],"additions":112,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pkg/result/results_test.go","lines":["@@ -268,3 +268,68 @@ func TestUpdateHostOS(t *testing.T) {"," \tgot[\"192.0.2.1\"].OSDetails = \"changed\""," \tassert.Equal(t, want, snapshot()[\"192.0.2.1\"])"," }","+","+func TestClosedPorts(t *testing.T) {","+\tres := NewResult()","+\tssh := &port.Port{Port: 22, Protocol: protocol.TCP}","+\tweb := &port.Port{Port: 80, Protocol: protocol.TCP}","+","+\tres.AddClosedPort(\"203.0.113.7\", ssh)","+\tres.AddClosedPort(\"203.0.113.7\", web)","+\tres.AddPort(\"203.0.113.7\", web)","+\tres.AddClosedPort(\"203.0.113.7\", web)","+\tres.AddPort(\"203.0.113.7\", &port.Port{Port: 53, Protocol: protocol.UDP})","+","+\tclosed := res.GetClosedPorts()","+\tassert.Len(t, closed[\"203.0.113.7\"], 1, \"an open reply wins over a reset either way round\")","+\tassert.Equal(t, 22, closed[\"203.0.113.7\"][0].Port)","+\tassert.False(t, res.IPHasPort(\"203.0.113.7\", ssh), \"closed ports stay out of the open set\")","+\tassert.Equal(t, map[string]int{\"203.0.113.7\": 1}, res.GetTCPPortCounts())","+}","+","+func TestClosedPortsBitset(t *testing.T) {","+\tres := NewResult()","+\tconst ip = \"203.0.113.8\"","+","+\tfor _, n := range []int{65535, 0, 1, 64, 63, 22} {","+\t\tres.AddClosedPort(ip, &port.Port{Port: n, Protocol: protocol.TCP})","+\t}","+\t// duplicates, udp and out of range ports add nothing","+\tres.AddClosedPort(ip, &port.Port{Port: 22, Protocol: protocol.TCP})","+\tres.AddClosedPort(ip, &port.Port{Port: 53, Protocol: protocol.UDP})","+\tres.AddClosedPort(ip, &port.Port{Port: 65536, Protocol: protocol.TCP})","+\tres.AddClosedPort(ip, &port.Port{Port: -1, Protocol: protocol.TCP})","+\tres.AddClosedPort(ip, nil)","+","+\tvar got []int","+\tfor _, p := range res.GetClosedPorts()[ip] {","+\t\tassert.Equal(t, protocol.TCP, p.Protocol)","+\t\tgot = append(got, p.Port)","+\t}","+\tassert.Equal(t, []int{0, 1, 22, 63, 64, 65535}, got, \"ports come back in order\")","+","+\t// SetPorts and AddPort both turn a closed port into an open one","+\tres.SetPorts(ip, []*port.Port{{Port: 22, Protocol: protocol.TCP}})","+\tres.AddPort(ip, &port.Port{Port: 64, Protocol: protocol.TCP})","+\tgot = nil","+\tfor _, p := range res.GetClosedPorts()[ip] {","+\t\tgot = append(got, p.Port)","+\t}","+\tassert.Equal(t, []int{0, 1, 63, 65535}, got)","+}","+","+func TestMergeClosedPorts(t *testing.T) {","+\tfrom := NewResult()","+\tfrom.AddClosedPort(\"203.0.113.9\", &port.Port{Port: 22, Protocol: protocol.TCP})","+\tfrom.AddClosedPort(\"203.0.113.9\", &port.Port{Port: 80, Protocol: protocol.TCP})","+\tfrom.AddClosedPort(\"203.0.113.10\", &port.Port{Port: 25, Protocol: protocol.TCP})","+","+\tinto := NewResult()","+\tinto.AddPort(\"203.0.113.9\", &port.Port{Port: 80, Protocol: protocol.TCP})","+\tinto.MergeClosedPorts(from)","+","+\tclosed := into.GetClosedPorts()","+\tassert.Len(t, closed[\"203.0.113.9\"], 1, \"a port the destination holds open is not merged as closed\")","+\tassert.Equal(t, 22, closed[\"203.0.113.9\"][0].Port)","+\tassert.Len(t, closed[\"203.0.113.10\"], 1)","+}"],"additions":65,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pkg/runner/options.go","lines":["@@ -105,6 +105,7 @@ type Options struct {"," \tHealthCheck       bool"," \tOnlyHostDiscovery bool // Perform only host discovery"," \tShowDeadHosts     bool // Report hosts that did not respond to discovery","+\tPortState         bool // Report closed and filtered TCP ports too"," \t// Deprecated: use WithHostDiscovery instead"," \tSkipHostDiscovery bool // Skip Host discovery"," \tWithHostDiscovery bool // Enable Host discovery","@@ -252,6 +253,7 @@ func ParseOptions() *Options {"," \t\tflagSet.StringVarP(&options.XMLOutput, \"xml-output\", \"oX\", \"\", \"write nmap-compatible XML output to file (- for stdout)\"),"," \t\tflagSet.StringVarP(&options.GrepOutput, \"grep-output\", \"oG\", \"\", \"write nmap-compatible greppable output to file (- for stdout)\"),"," \t\tflagSet.StringVarP(&options.OutputAll, \"output-all\", \"oA\", \"\", \"write json, xml and greppable output to <basename>.{json,xml,gnmap}\"),","+\t\tflagSet.BoolVar(&options.PortState, \"port-state\", false, \"also report closed and filtered tcp ports\"),"," \t)"," "," \tflagSet.CreateGroup(\"c